The prompt strings in prompts.py are copied verbatim (checked by sha256 in tests/rl/test_web_judge.py).
The parsing and scoring rules in judge.py follow the upstream code line by line. The Online-Mind2Web task
data (CC BY 4.0) is not vendored here.

WebJudge-7B (https://huggingface.co/osunlp/WebJudge-7B, Apache-2.0, fine-tuned from Qwen2.5-VL-7B-Instruct)
is downloaded at run time by kaggle/web-judge/run.py. Its weights are not part of this repository.

Deviations from upstream (also in docs/specs/web_judge.md):
  1. o4-mini request parameters. Upstream OpenaiEngine.generate sends max_tokens=512, temperature=0. The
     OpenAI API refuses both for o-series reasoning models. We send max_completion_tokens (default 8192,
     which covers reasoning plus the visible answer) and no temperature. The default reasoning effort is
     kept. The WebJudge-7B backend sends upstream's max_tokens=512, temperature=0 unchanged.
  2. Errors. Upstream retries 3 times and then lets the exception kill the worker. We retry 3 times
     (expo backoff) and then record the episode as judge_error, so the rest of the run continues.
  3. Screenshot files. v1 order is upstream's (first integer in the file name). We list only image files
     (.png/.jpg/.jpeg/.webp), so a stray .DS_Store or log no longer crashes. A v2 step whose screenshot
     is null (allowed for TASK_COMPLETE) is skipped; upstream would crash on it.
  4. JPEG encoding. Upstream converts only RGBA to RGB before saving as JPEG, so P/LA/CMYK images crash.
     We convert every mode other than RGB/L. RGB and RGBA inputs give the same bytes as upstream.
  5. Harness status. Episodes that result.json marks blocked or infra_error are counted as failures, as
     upstream would count them (success = verdict over all task dirs), but by default they are not sent to
     the judge (--judge-blocked sends them) and are reported separately.
  6. Cost cap. --max-usd stops the run before a call that could exceed the cap. Unfinished episodes are
     reported as not_judged; upstream has no cap.
  Everything else is unchanged: key-point parsing, the per-image 1-5 score regex, score_threshold=3,
  MAX_IMAGE=50, the "image/png" data-URL label on the JPEG key screenshots, the prompt without images
  when none pass the threshold, and success = "success" after "Status:" in the final answer.
